-- title:
--   Universal deformation ring topologically generated by Frobenius traces
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain and is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over the residue field $k$ of $\mathcal O$ (a $k$-vector space of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$, realised as $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms over $\mathbb Q$, to its $k$-endomorphisms, trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and let $\mathcal D$ be a predicate on adic Galois representations over local $\mathcal O$-algebras. Let $D$ be a [`GaloisRep.DeformationRingData`](def/GaloisRep_DeformationRingData.html#L8) for $\mathcal O$, $\bar\rho$ and $\mathcal D$: a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $D.R$ whose structure map is local and induces a surjection onto its residue field, together with absolute irreducibility of $\bar\rho$, a rank-$2$ adic representation $D.\rho$ over $D.R$ satisfying $\mathcal D$ whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$, and the universal property that any such representation of type $\mathcal D$ over such an algebra $A$ with residual representation equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ arises, up to equivalence, from $D.\rho$ by base change along a unique local $\mathcal O$-algebra map $D.R\to A$. Assume $h\mathcal D$: for every complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $A$ with local structure map inducing a surjection onto the residue field, and every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $f\colon D.R\to A$ which is a local homomorphism, the base change of $D.\rho$ along $f$ satisfies $\mathcal D$. Then for every finite set $S$ of natural numbers, every $n\in\mathbb N$ and every $x\in D.R$ there exists $b$ in the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $D.R$ generated by the set of elements of the form $\operatorname{tr} D.\rho(\sigma)$ — where $\ell$ is a prime not in $S$, $P$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ as the $\ell$-th power map — such that $x-b\in\mathfrak m_{D.R}^{\,n}$.
--
--   This is the assertion that a universal deformation ring of an absolutely irreducible residual representation is topologically generated over $\mathcal O$, for the maximal-adic topology, by the traces of Frobenius elements at the primes outside any prescribed finite set. It is used on the Galois side of the Taylor–Wiles construction, in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_flat) and [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_deformationRing_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary), to propagate compatibilities known at Frobenius traces to the whole deformation ring.
